      "evidence": "Wiping at 2:50 precedes the start of eating at 3:00. The two events both happened yesterday, but their relative order is still before.",
      "explanation": "食べるまえに puts wiping before eating. Use the dictionary form 食べる before まえ even though the main action ふいた is past. 食べたあとに would put wiping after eating, reversing the given order. The answer is the verb plus まえ; do not repeat the supplied に.",
